+# Retry credit reservation contract
+
+## Scope
+
+Internal application-service contract. No HTTP, GraphQL, or message-bus convention exists in this workspace, so this document does not invent an external endpoint.
+
+## Shared result
+
+`ReservationResult`: `reservation_id`, `workspace_id`, `attempt_key`, `status`, `credit_amount`, optional `provider_correlation_id`, optional `terminal_reason`, and `idempotent_replay`.
+
+## Operations
+
+### `reserveRetryCredit`
+
+**Input**: trusted `workspace_id`, stable `attempt_key`.  
+**Success**: atomically decrement one available credit and create `reserved`.  
+**Replay**: return existing reservation, with no second decrement.  
+**Exhausted**: return a distinct quota-exhausted result; do not invoke the provider.
+
+### `finalizeRetryCredit`
+
+**Input**: trusted workspace, attempt key, optional provider correlation after acceptance.  
+**Success**: conditionally change `reserved → finalized` once; balance stays charged.  
+**Replay/conflict**: return terminal record; never alter a released record.
+
+### `releaseRetryCredit`
+
+**Input**: trusted workspace, attempt key, reason `provider_failed`, `timed_out`, or `cancelled`.  
+**Success**: conditionally change `reserved → released` and re-credit one in the same transaction.  
+**Replay/conflict**: return terminal record; never alter a finalized record.
+
+### `dispatchReminderRetry`
+
+1. Reserve before provider I/O.
+2. Skip provider I/O when quota is exhausted.
+3. Invoke provider outside transaction, using attempt key as provider idempotency key when supported.
+4. Finalize on acceptance; release on failure, timeout, or cancellation.
+5. Route callback redelivery through the same terminal operations.
+
+## Error semantics
+
+| Condition | Result |
+|-----------|--------|
+| Unknown/mismatched workspace or callback correlation | Reject and audit; no mutation. |
+| Duplicate terminal callback | Existing terminal result with `idempotent_replay=true`. |
+| Conflicting terminal callback | Persisted terminal result remains authoritative; no mutation. |
+| Interruption after reserve | Recovery resolves durable reservation through the same service operations. |
+
+## Contract-test obligations
+
+- One credit plus two concurrent distinct attempts yields one reservation and no negative balance.
+- Replayed reserve does not debit twice.
+- Accepted flow finalizes without re-credit.
+- Failed, timed-out, and cancelled flows release once.
+- Replayed and racing terminal signals produce one terminal effect.
