+# S004 Provider retry quota — Data model
+
+## Scope
+
+This logical model supplies durable, exactly-once accounting. Concrete types and migration syntax wait for the repository's actual runtime and persistence conventions.
+
+## Entities
+
+### WorkspaceRetryQuota
+
+| Field | Type | Rules |
+|-------|------|-------|
+| `workspace_id` | stable workspace identifier | Primary key; trusted dispatch context determines it. |
+| `available_retry_credits` | non-negative integer | Must remain `>= 0`; reservation decrements and release increments it. |
+| `updated_at` | timestamp | Updated with each balance mutation. |
+
+### RetryCreditReservation
+
+| Field | Type | Rules |
+|-------|------|-------|
+| `reservation_id` | stable identifier | Primary key. |
+| `workspace_id` | identifier | References its workspace quota. |
+| `attempt_key` | opaque key | Unique with workspace; stable across retries and callbacks. |
+| `credit_amount` | integer | Fixed positive value `1` for S004. |
+| `status` | enum | `reserved`, `finalized`, or `released`. |
+| `provider_correlation_id` | nullable opaque id | Stored when the provider supplies one. |
+| `terminal_reason` | nullable | Required for release: `provider_failed`, `timed_out`, or `cancelled`. |
+| `created_at`, `terminal_at` | timestamps | Terminal timestamp is written once. |
+
+## Relationships and state machine
+
+- One workspace quota has many reservations.
+- Unique `(workspace_id, attempt_key)` binds duplicate requests to one reservation.
+
+```
+new --reserve--> reserved --accepted--> finalized
+                    └--failed / timeout / cancelled--> released
+```
+
+`finalized` and `released` are immutable terminal states. A duplicate reserve returns the existing record. A duplicate terminal call returns the persisted result; a conflicting terminal signal changes neither status nor balance.
+
+## Transactional invariants
+
+1. Reserve conditionally decrements a balance only when it is at least one and inserts `reserved` in the same transaction; otherwise neither mutation occurs.
+2. Finalize conditionally moves only `reserved → finalized`; it does not alter balance.
+3. Release conditionally moves only `reserved → released` and increments the balance by one in the same transaction.
+4. Provider I/O occurs outside transactions. Recovery resolves any stale reservation through the release/finalize boundary, never a direct balance edit.
+
+## Validation and migration notes
+
+- Reject non-positive credit amounts and blank/changing attempt keys.
+- Reject callback workspace/correlation mismatches without mutation.
+- Add non-negative-balance and unique-attempt constraints before enabling dispatch.
+- If a quota/ledger model already exists when implementation begins, extend it rather than create a second balance authority.
