+## Summary
+
+Wrap each reminder provider retry in a durable, transactional credit reservation. Reserve one workspace credit before dispatch; on provider acceptance finalize it, and on failure, timeout, or cancellation release it. A stable attempt key plus conditional transitions prevents duplicate callbacks and concurrent attempts from double-changing the balance.
+
+## Technical Approach
+
+Create one retry-quota domain boundary with reserve, finalize, and release operations. In one datastore transaction, reserve conditionally decrements a workspace balance only when it is at least one and inserts a `reserved` record keyed by the retry attempt. The dispatcher calls the provider only after that transaction commits. Finalize and release use compare-and-set transitions from `reserved`; release increments the balance in the same transaction as its transition. Repeated calls return the existing durable result without a second debit or credit. Use the attempt key as the provider idempotency key whenever the adapter supports one. This is a backend-only story; `/story-ui-spec` is not required.
+
+## Dependencies
+
+- Requires: a transactional persistent store; an existing/future reminder dispatcher; a stable retry-attempt identifier; and a provider adapter that reports accepted, failed, timed-out, and cancelled outcomes.
+- Provides: a reusable quota-reservation boundary for later reminder work.
+
+## Testing Strategy
+
+- Unit tests: state transitions, invalid transitions, and duplicate-operation results.
+- Integration tests: accepted, failed, timed-out, and cancelled provider outcomes plus callback redelivery.
+- Concurrency test: two distinct attempts against one remaining credit using a real transactional datastore.
+- Contract tests: the service operations in [retry-credit-reservation.md](contracts/retry-credit-reservation.md).
+
