+# S004 Provider retry quota — Validation scenarios
+
+## Preconditions
+
+1. A workspace begins with one available retry credit.
+2. A deterministic provider fake produces accepted, failed, timed-out, cancelled, and duplicate-callback outcomes.
+3. Concurrency scenarios use a real transactional datastore, not an in-memory counter.
+
+## Scenarios
+
+### Reserve before provider send
+
+Pause the provider after dispatch begins. Verify one durable `reserved` record and zero credits before provider completion. Verify no provider call occurs if reservation reports quota exhaustion.
+
+### Accepted provider send
+
+Return acceptance. Verify `reserved → finalized`, balance remains zero, and an acceptance replay changes nothing.
+
+### Failed, timed-out, and cancelled sends
+
+Run each outcome independently. Verify `reserved → released`, its reason is persisted, balance returns to one, and replay does not increment again.
+
+### Concurrent distinct attempts
+
+Start two attempt keys concurrently with one credit. Verify exactly one reservation/provider call, one quota-exhausted result, and no negative balance.
+
+### Duplicate reserve and terminal race
+
+Start the same attempt key twice; verify one reservation/debit. Race acceptance against failure; verify one terminal status, exactly its one balance effect, and no mutation from the later conflicting callback.
+
+### Untrusted callback correlation
+
+Attempt a terminal transition with mismatched workspace or provider correlation. Verify rejection/audit and unchanged reservation/balance.
+
+## Evidence for `/story-validate`
+
+- Output from all scenarios, including the real concurrent-datastore run.
+- Before/after reservation and quota values for duplicate and contention tests.
+- Provider-fake log proving quota exhaustion prevents provider dispatch.
+- An observable record of duplicate/conflicting callbacks with unchanged balance.
